    ## Manual Verification Steps for Iteration 0

    ### Prerequisites
    ```bash
    # Ensure services are running
    cd /Users/basicthinker/Projects/ddms-claude/claude
    docker compose up -d
    ```

    ### 1. Health Endpoints Verification

    **Test system health endpoint:**
    ```bash
    curl http://localhost:8000/health
    ```
    **Expected:** `{"status":"ok","env":"development"}`

    **Test API health endpoint:**
    ```bash
    curl http://localhost:8000/api/health
    ```
    **Expected:** `{"status":"ok","env":"development"}` (should match root health)

    **Test version endpoint:**
    ```bash
    curl http://localhost:8000/api/version
    ```
    **Expected:** `{"version":"0.1.0"}` (no environment field)

    ### 2. API Documentation

    **Open Swagger UI in browser:**
    ```
    http://localhost:8000/docs
    ```
    **Verify:**
    - Page loads with "DDMS API" title
    - Three endpoints visible under "health" tag
    - Can expand and test each endpoint interactively
    - Descriptions are clear and accurate

    **Open ReDoc in browser:**
    ```
    http://localhost:8000/redoc
    ```
    **Verify:**
    - Clean documentation interface loads
    - All three endpoints documented

    **Check OpenAPI schema:**
    ```bash
    curl http://localhost:8000/openapi.json | python3 -m json.tool
    ```
    **Verify:**
    - Valid JSON structure
    - Contains info.title: "DDMS API"
    - Contains info.description: "Device Data Monitoring System"
    - Contains info.version: "0.1.0"
    - All three paths defined: /health, /api/health, /api/version

    ### 3. Database Migration

    **Run migration on fresh database:**
    ```bash
    cd backend
    source .venv/bin/activate
    alembic upgrade head
    ```
    **Expected:**
    - No errors
    - Output shows "Running upgrade  -> 40646a8b5999, Initial empty migration"

    **Verify current migration:**
    ```bash
    alembic current
    ```
    **Expected:** `40646a8b5999 (head)`

    **Downgrade and upgrade again:**
    ```bash
    alembic downgrade base
    alembic upgrade head
    ```
    **Expected:** Both commands succeed without errors

    ### 4. Configuration & Logging

    **Check environment-based settings:**
    ```bash
    # Backend logs should show startup message
    docker compose logs backend | grep "Starting DDMS API"
    ```
    **Expected:** JSON-formatted log entry with version and environment

    **Test different log format (optional):**
    ```bash
    # Stop backend
    docker compose stop backend

    # Edit claude/.env to add: LOG_FORMAT=text
    echo "LOG_FORMAT=text" >> .env

    # Restart and check logs
    docker compose up -d backend
    docker compose logs backend --tail 10
    ```
    **Expected:** Human-readable text format logs instead of JSON

    ### 5. Test Suite

    **Run all tests:**
    ```bash
    cd backend
    source .venv/bin/activate
    pytest -v
    ```
    **Expected:**
    - 6 tests pass (3 unit + 3 integration)
    - No failures or errors
    - Coverage report shows ddms module coverage

    **Run tests with coverage:**
    ```bash
    pytest --cov=ddms --cov-report=term --cov-report=html
    ```
    **Expected:**
    - Coverage report displays
    - HTML report generated in `htmlcov/`

    **Run specific test categories:**
    ```bash
    pytest tests/unit/ -v          # Unit tests only
    pytest tests/integration/ -v   # Integration tests only
    ```

    ### 6. Code Quality Checks

    **Run linter:**
    ```bash
    cd backend
    source .venv/bin/activate
    ruff check ddms tests
    ```
    **Expected:** No linting errors

    **Check formatting:**
    ```bash
    ruff format --check ddms tests
    ```
    **Expected:** "All files would be left unchanged"

    **Run type checker:**
    ```bash
    mypy ddms
    ```
    **Expected:** "Success: no issues found"

    ### 7. Service Restart Verification

    **Test data persistence:**
    ```bash
    # Restart all services
    docker compose restart

    # Wait a few seconds
    sleep 5

    # Verify endpoints still work
    curl http://localhost:8000/health
    ```
    **Expected:** Services start cleanly and endpoints respond correctly

